# url-parser

CLI tool that parses and analyzes URLs, displaying protocol, host, path, query parameters, and more.

## Features

- Parse any URL into its components
- Display protocol, host, port, path, query parameters, fragment, and user info
- Three output formats: `text`, `table`, and `json`
- Single binary, no dependencies
- Built with Go

## Installation

### From source

```bash
go install github.com/TataneSan/url-parser@latest
```

### Build manually

```bash
git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/url-parser.git
cd url-parser
go build -o url-parser .
```

## Usage

```bash
url-parser <URL>
url-parser <URL> --format <text|table|json>
```

### Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--format` | Output format: `text` (default), `table`, or `json` |
| `-h, --help` | Show help message |

## Examples

### Text output (default)

```
$ url-parser "https://example.com/path?key=value"
URL: https://example.com/path?key=value
Valid: true
Protocol: https
Host: example.com
Path: /path
Query Parameters:
  key = value
```

### Table output

```
$ url-parser "https://api.github.com/repos?sort=updated&page=1" --format table
  URL          https://api.github.com/repos?sort=updated&page=1
  Valid        true
  Protocol     https
  Host         api.github.com
  Path         /repos
  Query: sort  updated
  Query: page  1
```

### JSON output

```
$ url-parser "https://user:pass@example.com:8080/page#section" --format json
{
  "original": "https://user:pass@example.com:8080/page#section",
  "valid": true,
  "protocol": "https",
  "host": "example.com",
  "port": "8080",
  "path": "/page",
  "fragment": "section",
  "user": "user",
  "has_password": true
}
```

### Invalid URL

```
$ url-parser "not a valid url"
Invalid URL: not a valid url
```

## License

MIT
