# dotenv-cli

CLI tool to read, write, and validate .env files.

## Features

- Parse and display .env file contents
- Get a specific variable value
- Set or update key-value pairs
- Validate .env files for common issues (empty values, duplicates, invalid keys)
- Export as shell `export` commands
- Single binary, no dependencies
- Built with Go

## Installation

### From source

```bash
go install github.com/TataneSan/dotenv-cli@latest
```

### Build manually

```bash
git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/dotenv-cli.git
cd dotenv-cli
go build -o dotenv-cli .
```

## Usage

```bash
dotenv-cli <file.env>
dotenv-cli <file.env> --get <KEY>
dotenv-cli <file.env> --set <KEY> <VALUE>
dotenv-cli <file.env> --validate
dotenv-cli <file.env> --export
```

### Options

| Flag | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `--get <KEY>` | Get the value of a specific key |
| `--set <KEY> <V>` | Set or update a key-value pair |
| `--validate` | Validate the .env file for issues |
| `--export` | Output as shell export commands |
| `-h, --help` | Show help message |

## Examples

### List all variables

```
$ dotenv-cli .env
KEY                            VALUE                LINE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
DB_HOST                        localhost            1
DB_PORT                        5432                 2
API_KEY                        abc123               3
```

### Get a specific value

```
$ dotenv-cli .env --get DB_HOST
localhost
```

### Set or update a value

```
$ dotenv-cli .env --set DB_PORT 3306
Set DB_PORT=3306
```

### Validate

```
$ dotenv-cli .env --validate
Found 1 issue(s):

  line 5: EMPTY_VAR has empty value
```

### Export as shell commands

```
$ dotenv-cli .env --export
export DB_HOST='localhost'
export DB_PORT='5432'
export API_KEY='abc123'
```

