+# json-schema-validator
+
+A fast, zero-dependency CLI tool for validating JSON data against JSON Schema. Written in Go.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Zero dependencies** — single binary, no external libraries
+- **JSON Schema Draft 7 support** — type, required, properties, additionalProperties, items, enum, const, minimum/maximum, minLength/maxLength, pattern, format, anyOf, allOf, oneOf, not, uniqueItems, min/maxItems, min/maxProperties, multipleOf
+- **Format validation** — email, uri, date-time, date, time, ipv4, ipv6, uuid, hostname
+- **Multiple input modes** — file, stdin pipe
+- **Multiple output modes** — human-readable errors, JSON output
+- **Exit codes** — 0 (valid), 1 (invalid), 2 (usage error)
+- **Portable** — single static binary
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-schema-validator@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-schema-validator.git
+cd json-schema-validator
+go build -o json-schema-validator .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-schema-validator <schema.json> <data.json>
+json-schema-validator <schema.json> -    # read data from stdin
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+| `-q, --quiet` | Only output errors, no success message |
+| `-j, --json` | Output errors in JSON format |
+
+### Exit codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|------|---------|
+| 0 | Validation passed |
+| 1 | Validation failed |
+| 2 | Usage or file error |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Basic validation
+
+```bash
+json-schema-validator schema.json data.json
+```
+
+### Pipe data from stdin
+
+```bash
+echo '{"name": "Alice", "age": 30}' | json-schema-validator schema.json -
+```
+
+### JSON error output
+
+```bash
+json-schema-validator -j schema.json data.json
+```
+
+### Use in CI/CD scripts
+
+```bash
+if ! json-schema-validator -q schema.json data.json; then
+  echo "Invalid data!" >&2
