+# netstat-go
+
+A fast CLI tool for viewing network connections and listening ports. Written in Go.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Zero dependencies** — single binary, no external libraries
+- **View connections** — TCP and UDP connections with state information
+- **Filter by protocol** — TCP only, UDP only, or both
+- **Filter by port** — show connections on a specific port
+- **Multiple output modes** — table, JSON, summary
+- **IPv4/IPv6 support** — filter by IP version
+- **Exit codes** — 0 (success), 1 (error)
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/netstat-go@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/netstat-go.git
+cd netstat-go
+go build -o netstat-go .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+netstat-go                    # show all connections
+netstat-go -t / --tcp         # show TCP connections only
+netstat-go -u / --udp         # show UDP connections only
+netstat-go -4 / --ip4         # show IPv4 connections only
+netstat-go -6 / --ip6         # show IPv6 connections only
+netstat-go -j / --json        # output as JSON
+netstat-go -s / --summary     # show connection summary
+netstat-go -p <port>          # filter by port number
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+| `-t, --tcp` | Show only TCP connections |
+| `-u, --udp` | Show only UDP connections |
+| `-4, --ip4` | Show only IPv4 connections |
+| `-6, --ip6` | Show only IPv6 connections |
+| `-j, --json` | Output as JSON |
+| `-s, --summary` | Show connection summary |
+| `-p, --port` | Filter by port number |
+
+### Exit codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|------|---------|
+| 0 | Success |
+| 1 | Error |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Show all connections
+
+```bash
+netstat-go
+```
+
+### Show TCP connections only
+
+```bash
+netstat-go -t
+```
+
+### Show connections on port 80
