 # netstat-cli
 
-Network connection monitor for the terminal. Displays active TCP/UDP connections with filtering, sorting, and real-time monitoring.
+Display active network connections from the terminal with filtering support.
+
+A lightweight Go CLI tool that reads `/proc/net/*` to show TCP/UDP connections, listening sockets, and connection states — without requiring root privileges or external dependencies.
 
 ## Features
 
-- Read connections from `/proc/net/tcp`, `/proc/net/tcp6`, `/proc/net/udp`, `/proc/net/udp6`
-- Color-coded connection states (ESTABLISHED=green, LISTEN=cyan, TIME_WAIT=yellow, etc.)
-- Filter by protocol, port, IP address, or connection state
-- Sort by state, local port, remote port, or protocol
-- Real-time monitoring mode with configurable refresh interval
-- Connection summary with counts per state
+- Display all active network connections (TCP/UDP)
