+# calendar-cli
+
+Display a calendar in the terminal. Supports single month, full year, quarter view, and relative navigation (next/previous N months).
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/calendar-cli@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/calendar-cli.git
+cd calendar-cli
+go build -o calendar-cli .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+calendar-cli                          # current month
+calendar-cli -y 2026                  # all months of 2026
+calendar-cli -m 3 -y 2026             # March 2026
+calendar-cli -m jan                   # January of current year
+calendar-cli -q 2 -y 2026             # Q2 2026 (Apr, May, Jun)
+calendar-cli -n 3                     # next 3 months
+calendar-cli -p 2                     # previous 2 months
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-y int` | Year (default: current year) |
+| `-m int\|str` | Month (1-12 or name/abbreviation) |
+| `-q int` | Quarter (1-4) |
+| `-n int` | Show next N months |
+| `-p int` | Show previous N months |
+| `-compact` | Compact output without colors |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Current month with today highlighted
+calendar-cli
+
+# Specific month
+calendar-cli -m 12 -y 2025
+calendar-cli -m dec -y 2025
+
+# Full year view
+calendar-cli -y 2026
+
+# Quarter view
+calendar-cli -q 1 -y 2026
+
+# Next 6 months
+calendar-cli -n 6
+
+# Previous 3 months (compact)
+calendar-cli -p 3 -compact
+```
+
+## Features
+
+- Color-coded weekdays (weekends in red)
+- Today's date highlighted
+- Quarter and full-year views
+- Compact mode for piping to other tools
+- Monday-first week layout
+
+## License
+
+MIT
