+# tcp-dump-lite
+
+A lightweight network traffic capture and analysis tool. View active connections, monitor bandwidth, and scan ports — all from the command line.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Active connections** — View all TCP/UDP connections with colored states
+- **Connection summary** — Visual breakdown of connection states with bar chart
+- **Interface stats** — Network interface traffic statistics (RX/TX bytes and packets)
+- **Bandwidth monitor** — Real-time bandwidth monitoring with configurable duration
+- **Port scanner** — Scan open ports on a host with batch processing
+- **Filtering** — Filter connections by IP, port, or state
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Clone and link
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/tcp-dump-lite.git
+cd tcp-dump-lite
+npm link
+
+# Or install globally
+npm install -g tcp-dump-lite
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+tcp-dump-lite <command> [options]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `connections [filter]` | Show active TCP/UDP connections |
+| `summary` | Show connection state summary |
+| `interfaces` | Show network interface statistics |
+| `monitor [duration]` | Monitor bandwidth in real-time (default: 10s) |
+| `scan <host> <ports>` | Scan open ports on a host |
+
+## Examples
+
+### View active connections
+
+```bash
+tcp-dump-lite connections
+tcp-dump-lite connections 8080
+tcp-dump-lite connections ESTABLISHED
+```
+
+### Connection summary
+
+```bash
+tcp-dump-lite summary
+```
+
+### Network interface stats
+
+```bash
+tcp-dump-lite interfaces
+```
+
+### Monitor bandwidth
+
+```bash
+tcp-dump-lite monitor 30
+```
+
+### Scan ports
+
+```bash
+tcp-dump-lite scan 127.0.0.1 22,80,443
+tcp-dump-lite scan 192.168.1.1 8080-8090
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
