+# release-notes
+
+Generate release notes from git tags and conventional commit messages. Supports markdown, plain text, and JSON output formats.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Conventional commit parsing**: Automatically categorizes commits by type (feat, fix, docs, refactor, test, chore)
+- **Multiple output formats**: Markdown, plain text, or JSON
+- **Grouped or flat output**: Group commits by type or list them chronologically
+- **Tag range selection**: Generate notes between any two tags or for unreleased commits
+- **Verbose mode**: Include full commit hashes and author information
+- **Zero dependencies**: Single binary, no external libraries
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/release-notes@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/release-notes.git
+cd release-notes
+go build -o release-notes .
+sudo mv release-notes /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+release-notes [OPTIONS]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-f, --format FORMAT` | Output format: `markdown` (default), `plain`, `json` |
+| `--ungrouped` | Don't group commits by type |
+| `-v, --verbose` | Include full commit hash and author info |
+| `--unreleased` | Generate notes for commits since last tag |
+| `--from TAG` | Starting tag (e.g., `v1.0.0`) |
+| `--to TAG` | Ending tag (e.g., `v1.1.0`) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Notes for last two tags (markdown, grouped)
+release-notes
+
+# Notes for commits since last tag
+release-notes --unreleased
+
+# Notes between specific tags
+release-notes --from v1.0.0 --to v1.1.0
+
+# Output as JSON
+release-notes -f json
+
+# Plain text, no grouping
+release-notes -f plain --ungrouped
+
+# Verbose with commit hashes
+release-notes -v
+```
+
+### Example output (markdown)
+
+```markdown
+## v1.1.0
+
+*Released: 2026-05-28*
+
+Compare with [previous release](v1.0.0...v1.1.0)
