+# webhook-monitor
+
+REST API for monitoring webhooks with automatic health checks and alerting on failures.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Webhook monitoring** — Periodically check webhooks with configurable intervals
+- **Automatic alerting** — Send alerts after consecutive failures to a configured URL
+- **Health check history** — Track check results with status, latency, and error details
+- **Configurable thresholds** — Set custom failure counts before triggering alerts
+- **In-memory storage** — Lightweight, no external dependencies
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### Webhook Management
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| POST | `/api/v1/webhooks` | Create a webhook monitor |
+| GET | `/api/v1/webhooks` | List all webhooks |
+| GET | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}` | Get a webhook |
+| PUT | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}` | Update a webhook |
+| DELETE | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}` | Delete a webhook |
+
+### Monitoring
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| GET | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}/results` | Get check results for a webhook |
+| GET | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}/alerts` | Get alerts for a webhook |
+| POST | `/api/v1/webhooks/{id}/test` | Trigger a manual check |
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/webhook-monitor@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone git@github.com:TataneSan/webhook-monitor.git
+cd webhook-monitor
+go build -o webhook-monitor .
+./webhook-monitor
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Start the server
+
+```bash
+./webhook-monitor
+# webhook-monitor starting on :8080
+```
+
+### Create a webhook monitor
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/webhooks \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "name": "my-api",
+    "url": "https://api.example.com/health",
+    "method": "GET",
+    "interval": 60,
+    "alert_url": "https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXX/YYY/ZZZ",
+    "alert_after": 3
+  }'
+```
+
+### Get check results
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8080/api/v1/webhooks/wh_1/results
+```
+
