+# redirect-api
+
+HTTP redirect API with click statistics and A/B testing support.
+
+Create short redirect endpoints, track clicks with browser/country/referrer stats, and run A/B tests by splitting traffic between multiple destination URLs with weighted variants.
+
+## Features
+
+- Create redirects with custom HTTP status codes (301, 302, 307, 308)
+- Optional expiration via duration string (e.g. `24h`, `720h`)
+- Click statistics: total hits, browser breakdown, referrers, countries
+- A/B testing: create variant groups with weighted traffic splitting
+- A/B test statistics: hits per variant, actual vs expected share
+- JSON persistence with periodic auto-save
+- Health check endpoint
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### Redirects
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/api/redirects` | List all redirects |
+| POST | `/api/redirects` | Create a redirect |
+| GET | `/api/redirects/{id}` | Get a redirect |
+| DELETE | `/api/redirects/{id}` | Delete a redirect |
+| GET | `/api/redirects/{id}/stats` | Get click stats for a redirect |
+
+### A/B Groups
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| POST | `/api/ab-groups` | Create an A/B test group |
+| GET | `/api/ab-groups/{id}` | Get an A/B group |
+| GET | `/api/ab-groups/{id}/stats` | Get A/B test statistics |
+
+### Redirect (user-facing)
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/r/{id}` | Perform the redirect (302 by default) |
+
+### System
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/health` | Health check |
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Run with Docker
+docker run -d -p 8080:8080 --name redirect-api tatanesan/redirect-api
+
+# Or build from source
+go build -o redirect-api .
+./redirect-api
+```
+
+Server starts on `http://localhost:8080`.
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Create a redirect
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/redirects \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "dest_url": "https://example.com/promo",
+    "code": 302,
+    "expires_in": "24h"
+  }'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
