+# config-validator
+
+Validate configuration files (JSON, YAML, TOML, INI) via HTTP API.
+
+Upload a config file or send content directly to get validation results with errors and warnings. Supports automatic format detection from file extension or content.
+
+## Features
+
+- Validate JSON, YAML, TOML, and INI configuration files
+- Upload files or send content via JSON
+- Automatic format detection from file extension
+- Detailed error messages with line numbers
+- Warnings for common issues (tabs in YAML, trailing commas, duplicate keys)
+- Health check endpoint
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### Validation
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| POST | `/api/validate` | Validate content from JSON body |
+| POST | `/api/validate-file` | Upload and validate a file |
+
+### System
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| GET | `/health` | Health check |
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Run with Docker
+docker run -d -p 8080:8080 --name config-validator tatanesan/config-validator
+
+# Or build from source
+go build -o config-validator .
+./config-validator
+```
+
+Server starts on `http://localhost:8080`.
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Validate JSON content
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/validate \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"my-app\",\n  \"port\": 8080\n}",
+    "format": "json"
+  }'
+```
+
+Response (valid):
+```json
+{
+  "file": "",
+  "valid": true,
+  "format": "json"
+}
+```
+
+### Validate YAML content
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/validate \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "content": "server:\n  port: 8080\n  host: localhost",
+    "format": "yaml"
+  }'
+```
+
+### Validate with errors
+
