+# config-validator
+
+Validate configuration files (JSON, YAML, TOML, INI) from the command line. Checks syntax, structure, and optional strict validation with warnings.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Multi-format support**: JSON, YAML, TOML, INI
+- **Auto-detection**: Automatically detects format when file extension is ambiguous
+- **Strict mode**: Additional checks for duplicate keys, empty keys, and structural issues
+- **Explicit format override**: Force a specific format with `--format`
+- **Exit codes**: `0` valid, `1` usage error, `2` validation failure — perfect for CI pipelines
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/config-validator@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/config-validator.git
+cd config-validator
+go build -o config-validator .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+config-validator [OPTIONS] <file>
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-s, --strict` | Enable strict validation with additional checks |
+| `-f, --format` | Specify format explicitly (`json`, `yaml`, `toml`, `ini`) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+| `-v, --version` | Show version |
+
+### Examples
+
+Validate a JSON file:
+```bash
+config-validator config.json
+```
+
+Strict validation on a YAML file:
+```bash
+config-validator --strict app.yaml
+```
+
+Force JSON format on a file without `.json` extension:
+```bash
+config-validator -f json config.txt
+```
+
+## Supported Formats
+
+| Format | Extensions |
+|--------|-----------|
+| JSON | `.json` |
+| YAML | `.yaml`, `.yml` |
+| TOML | `.toml` |
+| INI | `.ini`, `.cfg`, `.conf` |
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|------|---------|
+| 0 | File is valid |
+| 1 | Usage error (no file, bad arguments) |
+| 2 | Validation failure (invalid syntax) |
+
+## CI Integration
+
+```yaml
