+# secret-manager
+
+Encrypted local secrets manager for developers. Store sensitive values (API keys, passwords, tokens) in an AES-256 encrypted vault file, with CLI access and multiple export formats.
+
+## Features
+
+- **AES-256-GCM encryption**: secrets are encrypted at rest with a password-derived key
+- **Groups**: organize secrets into logical groups (database, api, staging, etc.)
+- **Multiple export formats**: env, dotenv, YAML
+- **Import from .env files**: bulk import KEY=VALUE pairs
+- **Search**: fuzzy search across keys and groups
+- **Single binary**: zero dependencies, works anywhere
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/secret-manager@latest
+```
+
+Or download the binary from [releases](https://github.com/TataneSan/secret-manager/releases).
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Set environment variable to avoid typing password each time
+export SECRET_MANAGER_PASSWORD="your-password"
+
+# Store a secret
+secret-manager set DB_PASSWORD supersecret123 --group database
+
+# Retrieve a secret
+secret-manager get DB_PASSWORD
+
+# List all secrets
+secret-manager list
+
+# Export as .env file
+secret-manager export --format dotenv > .env
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+| Command                              | Description                        |
+|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------|
+| `secret-manager set <KEY> [VALUE]`   | Set a secret value                 |
+| `secret-manager get <KEY>`           | Get a secret value                 |
+| `secret-manager delete <KEY>`        | Delete a secret                    |
+| `secret-manager list`                | List all secrets                   |
+| `secret-manager search <QUERY>`      | Search secrets by key or group     |
+| `secret-manager export [options]`    | Export secrets                     |
+| `secret-manager import <FILE>`       | Import secrets from a file         |
+| `secret-manager init`                | Initialize a new vault             |
+
+### Set
+
+```bash
+# Set with value argument
+secret-manager set API_KEY abc123 --group api
+
+# Set from stdin (safer for terminals)
+secret-manager set API_KEY < api_key.txt
+
+# Set from pipe
+echo "my-secret" | secret-manager set API_KEY
+```
+
+### Get
+
+```bash
+# Print the value
+secret-manager get API_KEY
+
+# Show metadata
+secret-manager get API_KEY --info
+```
+
+### List
+
