+# delay-api
+
+An API that simulates configurable response delays. Useful for testing timeout handling, retry logic, and latency scenarios in HTTP clients.
+
+## Features
+
+- Configurable delay via query parameter or path
+- Supports milliseconds, seconds, and minutes
+- Returns timing information (start, end, elapsed)
+- Configurable max delay to prevent abuse
+- CORS support
+- Streaming delay option (SSE)
+- Request logging
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/delay-api@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/delay-api.git
+cd delay-api
+go build -o delay-api .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+delay-api [flags]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `--host` | Bind address | `127.0.0.1` |
+| `--port` | Bind port | `8080` |
+| `--max-delay` | Maximum allowed delay | `30s` |
+| `--cors` | Enable CORS headers | `false` |
+| `--silent` | Suppress request logs | `false` |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+delay-api
+delay-api --max-delay 60s
+delay-api --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000 --cors
+```
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Path | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `/delay/:duration` | Delay response by duration (e.g. `/delay/2s`) |
+| `/` | Delay via `wait` query param (e.g. `/?wait=1s`) |
+| `/stream/:duration` | Server-sent events with delay |
+
+## Testing
+
+```bash
+# 1 second delay
+curl http://localhost:8080/delay/1s
+
+# 500ms delay
+curl http://localhost:8080/delay/500ms
+
+# Via query param
+curl "http://localhost:8080/?wait=2s"
+
+# Test timeout (will timeout after 1s)
+curl --max-time 1 http://localhost:8080/delay/5s
+```
+
+## Docker
+
