+# Echo Webhook
+
+Endpoint qui logue et retourne les webhooks reçus. Idéal pour tester et déboguer des webhooks entrants.
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+npm install
+```
+
+## Utilisation
+
+```bash
+# Lancement local
+npm start
+
+# Avec port personnalisé
+PORT=8080 npm start
+```
+
+L'API démarre sur `http://localhost:3000` par défaut.
+
+## Endpoints
+
+### `POST /hook/:path`
+
+Capture un webhook et le logue :
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/hook/github \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"event": "push", "repo": "my-project"}'
+```
+
+Réponse :
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "a1b2c3d4",
+  "logged": true,
+  "timestamp": "2026-05-28T12:00:00.000Z"
+}
+```
+
+### `GET /hooks`
+
+Liste les webhooks récents :
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:3000/hooks
+```
+
+Avec limite :
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:3000/hooks?limit=5
+```
+
+Réponse :
+
+```json
+{
+  "count": 3,
+  "webhooks": [
+    {
+      "id": "a1b2c3d4",
+      "method": "POST",
+      "url": "/hook/github",
+      "pathname": "/hook/github",
+      "query": {},
+      "headers": {
+        "host": "localhost:3000",
+        "content-type": "application/json"
+      },
+      "body": "{\"event\":\"push\",\"repo\":\"my-project\"}",
+      "timestamp": "2026-05-28T12:00:00.000Z",
+      "ip": "::1"
+    }
