+# Mock API Server
+
+A lightweight, configurable mock API server for testing. Define routes, responses, delays, and status codes via a simple JSON configuration file.
+
+## Features
+
+- Configure routes via JSON file
+- Support for all HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, ANY)
+- Custom status codes
+- Response delays (simulate slow endpoints)
+- Request body matching
+- Query parameter matching
+- Route hit limits (one-time mocks)
+- Template variables in responses (`{{METHOD}}`, `{{PATH}}`, `{{HOST}}`, `{{ORIGIN}}`)
+- Zero dependencies
+- Single file server
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+# Global install
+npm install -g mock-api
+
+# Or local install
+npm install mock-api
+```
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Start with default config
+mock-api
+
+# Custom port
+mock-api --port 8080
+
+# Custom config file
+mock-api --config ./my-routes.json
+```
+
+## Configuration
+
+Create a `config.json` file with your routes:
+
+```json
+{
+  "routes": [
+    {
+      "method": "GET",
+      "path": "/api/users",
+      "status": 200,
+      "body": {
+        "users": [
+          { "id": 1, "name": "Alice" },
+          { "id": 2, "name": "Bob" }
+        ]
+      }
+    },
+    {
+      "method": "POST",
+      "path": "/api/users",
+      "status": 201,
+      "body": { "message": "Created", "method": "TEMPLATE" }
+    },
+    {
+      "method": "GET",
+      "path": "/api/slow",
+      "status": 200,
+      "delay": 2000,
+      "body": { "message": "This was delayed" }
+    },
+    {
+      "method": "GET",
+      "path": "/api/error",
+      "status": 500,
+      "body": { "error": "Something went wrong" }
+    }
+  ]
