+# ip-api
+
+Lightweight REST API that returns detailed information about the client's IP address.
+
+Returns IP address, geolocation, ISP, ASN, and connection type in JSON format. Uses free geolocation data sources with no external dependencies required.
+
+## Features
+
+- Returns client IP address
+- Geolocation data (country, region, city, coordinates)
+- ISP and ASN information
+- Timezone and currency info
+- Supports JSON and plain text output
+- CORS enabled for browser usage
+- Docker-ready
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go build -o ip-api ./cmd/ip-api
+./ip-api --port 8080
+```
+
+### With Go install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/ip-api/cmd/ip-api@latest
+ip-api --port 8080
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker run -d -p 8080:8080 tatanesan/ip-api
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Start the server
+
+```bash
+./ip-api
+```
+
+### Options
+
+```
+  --port int     Port to listen on (default 8080)
+  --host string  Host to bind to (default "0.0.0.0")
+  --timeout int  HTTP timeout in seconds (default 10)
+```
+
+### API Endpoints
+
+#### GET /
+
+Returns full IP information as JSON.
+
+```bash
+curl http://localhost:8080/
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
+  "ip": "203.0.113.42",
+  "country": "France",
+  "country_code": "FR",
+  "region": "Ile-de-France",
+  "region_code": "IDF",
